        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-08-09 15:30:15.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-19954 tests: widen sanity-lnet router NI status wait",
        "message": "LU-19954 tests: widen sanity-lnet router NI status wait\n\ncheck_router_ni_status() waits alive_router_check_interval +\nrouter_ping_timeout for the router NIs to reach the expected state.\nThat is exactly the idle period a router requires before it marks an\nNI down, so the check has no slack. A single LNet ping received on the\nnet restarts that period, and the wait expires before the NI can go\ndown. Test nodes share a subnet and load LNet with accept=all, so an\nunrelated node reaching the router is enough to fail tests 222 to 225\nwith \"tcp should be down\".\n\nWait on a wall-clock deadline of three idle periods instead, which\ntolerates a ping arriving late in the wait. Tests that reach the\nexpected state still return as soon as they see it.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: If7c5f9f1dd35a954cfb2cfaaeb9c5da8e8f72895\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
